<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 935 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 935 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the  UK money market with a further 935 million stg of assistance at established  interest rates.</p>
<p>It allotted 28 million stg in bills outright and 907 million in repos  to August 14 and 18.</p>
<p>The Bank has now provided liquidity totalling 1.65 billion stg in  response to a revised money market shortage forecast of 1.8 billion  stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
</text>
